<title>INDIA: Little trade in India call money, most banks shut.</title>
<headline>Little trade in India call money, most banks shut.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's call money markets were inactive on Monday as most banks were closed for a local religious holiday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Only banks in the southern city of Madras are open.</p>
<p>On Friday, Indian call money was quoted in the 0.25-0.50 percent range. All banks reopen on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Bombay money desk +91-22-265 9000</p>
